      "traits": [
        "sonic"
      ],
      "text": "Grouloop utters a powerful croak that deals 6d10 sonic damage to any non-boggard within a 30-foot emanation (DC 27 basic Fortitude save save).\n\nA creature with the Frightened condition that fails its saving throw increases its frightened condition by 1 (on a critical failure, the creature is also Fleeing for as long as it is frightened).\n\nGrouloop can't use Soul-Shaking Croak again for 1d4 rounds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Swamp Stride",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Grouloop ignores difficult terrain caused by swamp terrain features."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Tongue Grab",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "If Grouloop hits a creature with her tongue, that creature becomes Grabbed. Unlike with a normal grab, the creature isn't Immobilized, but it can't move beyond the reach of Grouloop's tongue.\n\nA creature can sever the tongue by hitting AC 24 and dealing at least 9 slashing damage. Though this doesn't deal any damage to the boggard, it prevents her from using her tongue Strike until she regrows her tongue, which takes a week."
    },
